    {
      "page_title": "Defer and Recover",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where recover Works",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`recover()` stops a panic and returns its value",
            "Only when called directly inside a deferred function",
            "Outside a panic it returns `nil` and does nothing",
            "Not directly deferred? Also `nil`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "defer func() {",
            "  if r := recover(); r != nil {",
            "    err = fmt.Errorf(\"recovered: %v\", r)",
            "  }",
            "}()"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Converting a panic to an error needs a named return value",
            "An unnamed result cannot be reassigned from a defer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "defer Semantics",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arguments evaluate immediately; the call runs at function exit",
            "Closures capturing a loop variable were a trap before Go 1.22",
            "Defers run LIFO",
            "Each `defer` in a loop stacks until the function returns"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "for _, f := range files {",
            "  defer f.Close() // all run at func exit",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Execution Resumes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "panic(v)",
              "defers LIFO",
              "recover()",
              "caller resumes"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The function that deferred the recover returns to its caller — never to the panic site",
            "Recover cannot cross goroutines",
            "`go f()` panicking is not caught by the parent's recover",
            "Every goroutine you spawn needs its own recover"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Legitimate Boundaries",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HTTP server middleware",
            "Plugin and user-code boundaries",
            "Recursive parsers using panic for control flow",
            "Test helpers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "net/http Default",
          "items": [
            "Recovers panics per request",
            "Closes the connection",
            "Logs the stack to `Server.ErrorLog`",
            "Add middleware to answer with a 500"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "if r := recover(); r != nil {",
            "  if !isMine(r) { panic(r) } // re-panic",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Never Recover Blindly",
          "text": "Swallowing a nil-pointer panic leaves corrupted state running. Only absorb the signals you threw yourself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Error Traps and Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Typed-nil Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var p *MyErr = nil",
            "var e error = p",
            "fmt.Println(e != nil) // true, not nil!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An interface holds a type word and a value word",
            "A set type word makes it non-nil, even with a nil value",
            "Return `error`-typed variables, not concrete pointers",
            "`if err != nil { return err }` then `return nil`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shadowing and Log Noise",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`if err := f(); err != nil` hides the outer `err` inside the block",
            "The failure can vanish silently at the join point",
            "Do not log and return the same error — the caller logs it again",
            "Choose one boundary that logs: the top-level handler"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Closing and Ignoring",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "defer func() {",
            "  err = errors.Join(err, f.Close())",
            "}()"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`_ = f.Close()` is explicit and reviewable; a bare call is not",
            "`Close` can report late write errors (NFS, full disk)",
            "Plain `defer f.Close()` swallows that error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sets vs Trees",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "errors.Join",
                "lines": [
                  "parallel failures",
                  "validation results",
                  "flat set",
                  "Unwrap() []error"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "%w chain",
                "lines": [
                  "layered context",
                  "one cause per level",
                  "linear",
                  "Unwrap() error"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Retry decisions belong to behaviour, not identity",
            "Check `Timeout()` via `errors.As`; `Temporary()` is deprecated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "Data",
            "Coupling"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "sentinel",
              "none",
              "tight"
            ],
            [
              "custom type",
              "rich",
              "heavier API"
            ],
            [
              "opaque + behaviour",
              "via interface",
              "loosest"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "What It Costs",
          "text": "`errors.New` and `fmt.Errorf` allocate. Sentinel comparison does not. `As` pays for reflection. All irrelevant until it is in a loop."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Concurrency, Testing, Linting & Retry",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Concurrency and Tooling",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`errgroup.Group.Wait()` returns the first non-nil error",
            "`WithContext` groups also cancel ctx",
            "`context.Cause(ctx)` (Go 1.20+) gives the specific reason",
            "`ctx.Err()` gives only Canceled or DeadlineExceeded"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Test and Lint",
          "items": [
            "Assert with `errors.Is`/`errors.As`, never on strings",
            "`t.Fatalf` on an unexpected non-nil error",
            "`errcheck` — unchecked returns",
            "`errorlint` — `%v` misuse, `==` on errors",
            "`wrapcheck` — unwrapped errors from other packages"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Retry by Behaviour",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var ne net.Error",
            "if errors.As(err, &ne) &&",
            "  ne.Timeout() {",
            "  return retry() // behaviour, not identity",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "pass &ne, never ne"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`strings.Contains(err.Error(), ...)` — breaks on rewording",
            "Log **and** return — the same failure logged twice",
            "Bare `f.Close()` on a written file — write error lost"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
