    {
      "page_title": "Wrapping Rules & Panic Boundaries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Two Nevers",
          "text": "Never `==` an error, and never match on `err.Error()` text. Both break the first time someone wraps or rewords."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`err == io.EOF` after a layer wrapped it",
            "`%w` on a nil err — prints `%!w(<nil>)`",
            "A custom `Is` that always returns true"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "%w Is API",
          "text": "Wrapping exposes the cause to callers. If you might swap the implementation, wrap with `%v`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Implementing Wrappers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Unwrap() error` on wrapper types",
            "`Unwrap() []error` for multi-errors",
            "`Is`/`As` methods only for aliasing, never for logic",
            "`errors.Join` merges independent failures into a tree `Is`/`As` still walk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Boundaries",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`recover` only in a directly deferred closure",
            "Only at a real boundary, with a named return to convert",
            "Every `go` statement is a new panic domain",
            "Recover there or accept process death"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "go func() {",
            "  defer func() {",
            "    if r := recover(); r != nil {",
            "      log.Printf(\"panic: %v\", r) }",
            "  }()",
            "  work() }()"
          ],
          "note": "parent's recover never sees this"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Watch the typed-nil interface trap and error shadowing",
            "Both silently turn failures into successes",
            "One layer, one wrap, one log site",
            "Context accumulates without duplication"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "func check() error {",
            "  if bad { return &MyErr{} }",
            "  return nil // not a nil *MyErr",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "return untyped nil on success"
        }
      ]
    },
